" or \"a\"."],"rows":[["I","ego","EH-goh"],["you (one person)","tu","too"],["he / she / it","is / ea / id","is / EH-ah / id"],["we","nos","nohs"],["you all","vos","wohs"],["they","ei / eae / ea","EH-ee / EH-ai / EH-ah"]],"ex":[["I am a student","ego discipulus sum","EH-goh dis-KIP-oo-loos soom"],["you are tall","tu altus es","too AHL-toos ehs"],["she is my sister","ea soror mea est","EH-ah SOH-ror MEH-ah est"],["we are friends","nos amici sumus","nohs ah-MEE-kee SOO-moos"],["they are teachers","ei magistri sunt","EH-ee mah-GIS-tree soont"],["I am happy","laetus sum","LAI-toos soom"],["you all are late","vos seri estis","wohs SEH-ree ES-tis"],["he is a doctor","is medicus est","is MEH-di-koos est"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["A noun changes its ending to show its job in the sentence (case). The basic forms: puella, puellae (girl); dominus, domini (master); rex, reges (king); hortus, horti (garden). Learn each noun in two forms. Adjectives must agree with the noun."],"rows":[["girl, girls","puella, puellae","poo-EL-lah poo-EL-lai"],["master, masters","dominus, domini","DOH-mi-noos DOH-mi-nee"],["king, kings","rex, reges","reks REH-gehs"],["city, cities","urbs, urbes","oorbs OOR-behs"]],"ex":[["the boy","puer","POO-er"],["the girl","puella","poo-EL-lah"],["the books","libri","LEE-bree"],["a red house","domus rubra","DOH-moos ROO-brah"],["the cities","urbes","OOR-behs"],["one cat, two cats","una feles, duae felis","OO-nah FEH-lehs DOO-ai FEH-lehs"],["one pen, two pens","unus stilus, duo stili","OO-noos STEE-loos DOO-oh STEE-lee"],["a lesson, lessons","lectio, lectiones","LEK-tee-oh lek-tee-OH-nehs"],["a friend, friends","amicus, amici","ah-MEE-koos ah-MEE-kee"]]},{"id":"sum-to-be","title":"Sum: to be","text":["Sum is irregular. It works for both \"who/what\" and \"where/how\"."],"rows":[["I am","sum","soom"],["you are","es","ehs"],["he / she is","est","est"],["we are","sumus","SOO-moos"],["you all are","estis","ES-tis"],["they are","sunt","soont"]],"ex":[["I am English","Anglus sum","AHN-gloos soom"],["he is a doctor","medicus est","MEH-di-koos est"],["it is Monday","dies Lunae est","DEE-ehs LOO-nai est"],["we are from Uzbekistan","ex Uzbekistania sumus","eks ooz-beh-kis-TAH-nee-ah SOO-moos"],["they are tall","alti sunt","AHL-tee soont"],["I am at home","domi sum","DOH-mee soom"],["she is tired","fessa est","FES-sah est"],["where are you?","ubi es?","OO-bi ehs"],["we are well","bene valemus","BEH-neh wah-LEH-moos"],["the soup is cold","ius frigidum est","yoos FREE-gi-doom est"]]},{"id":"habeo-to-have","title":"Habeo: to have","text":["Habeo means \"I have\". You can also say \"mihi est\" (there is to me). Latin does not use \"to have\" for age or hunger: use \"annos natus sum\" (I was born so many years ago) and \"esurio\" (I am hungry)."],"rows":[["I have","habeo","hah-BEH-oh"],["you have","habes","HAH-behs"],["he / she has","habet","HAH-bet"],["we have","habemus","hah-BEH-moos"],["you all have","habetis","hah-BEH-tis"],["they have","habent","HAH-bent"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","fratrem habeo","FRAH-trem hah-BEH-oh"],["she has two cats","duas feles habet","DOO-ahs FEH-lehs HAH-bet"],["we have time","tempus habemus","TEM-poos hah-BEH-moos"],["I am hungry","esurio","eh-SOO-ree-oh"],["they have a car","autocinetum habent","ow-toh-KEE-neh-toom HAH-bent"],["there is a lesson today","hodie lectio est","HOH-dee-eh LEK-tee-oh est"],["there is no teacher","magister non est","mah-GIS-ter nohn est"],["I have a question","quaestionem habeo","kwai-STEE-oh-nem hah-BEH-oh"]]},{"id":"regular-verbs-present-tense","title":"Regular verbs (present tense)","text":["Latin verbs have four families. Take off the ending (-re) and add: -o, -s, -t, -mus, -tis, -nt. The vowel before the ending changes by family."],"rows":[["amare (to love): ego","amo","AH-moh"],["amare: tu","amas","AH-mahs"],["amare: is / ea","amat","AH-maht"],["amare: nos","amamus","ah-MAH-moos"],["amare: vos","amatis","ah-MAH-tis"],["amare: ei","amant","AH-mahnt"]],"ex":[["I speak English","Anglice loquor","AHN-gli-keh LOH-kwor"],["you eat a lot","multum edis","MOOL-toom EH-dis"],["she lives in Rome","Romae habitat","ROH-mai HAH-bi-taht"],["we work every day","cotidie laboramus","koh-TEE-dee-eh lah-boh-RAH-moos"],["they drink water","aquam bibunt","AH-kwahm BEE-boont"],["I read a book","librum lego","LEE-broom LEH-goh"],["you see the sea","mare vides","MAH-reh WEE-dehs"],["we hear music","musicam audimus","MOO-si-kahm ow-DEE-moos"]]},{"id":"eo-to-go","title":"Eo: to go","text":["Eo is irregular. To say \"I am going to do something\", Latin uses the future tense, not \"go + infinitive\"."],"rows":[["I go","eo","EH-oh"],["you go","is","ees"],["he / she goes","it","it"],["we go","imus","EE-moos"],["you all go","itis","EE-tis"],["they go","eunt","EH-oont"]],"ex":[["I am going to school","ad scholam eo","ad SKOH-lahm EH-oh"],["where are you going?","quo is?","kwoh ees"],["we are going to eat","cenabimus","keh-NAH-bi-moos"],["she is going to travel","iter faciet","I-ter FAH-kee-et"],["let us go!","eamus!","eh-AH-moos"],["they go home","domum eunt","DOH-moom EH-oont"],["I go to the market","ad forum eo","ad FOH-room EH-oh"],["he goes to Rome","Romam it","ROH-mahm it"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["Latin word order is flexible, because endings show who does what. The usual order is subject, object, verb (the verb last)."],"rows":[["subject + object + verb","ego panem edo","EH-goh PAH-nem EH-doh"],["adjective after or before the noun","canis niger / niger canis","KAH-nis NI-ger"],["place or time","hodie Romae laboro","HOH-dee-eh ROH-mai lah-BOH-roh"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","panem edo","PAH-nem EH-doh"],["Maria reads a book","Maria librum legit","mah-REE-ah LEE-broom LEH-git"],["we live in a big house","in magna domo habitamus","in MAHG-nah DOH-moh hah-bi-TAH-moos"],["he works here today","hodie hic laborat","HOH-dee-eh heek lah-BOH-raht"],["the dog is black","canis niger est","KAH-nis NI-ger est"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put \"non\" before the verb. \"Nihil\" = nothing, \"nemo\" = nobody, \"numquam\" = never. Always compare with the positive form."],"rows":[["not","non","nohn"],["nothing","nihil","NEE-hil"],["nobody","nemo","NEH-moh"],["never","numquam","NOOM-kwahm"]],"ex":[["I want","volo","WOH-loh"],["I do not want","nolo","NOH-loh"],["I speak English","Anglice loquor","AHN-gli-keh LOH-kwor"],["I do not speak English","Anglice non loquor","AHN-gli-keh nohn LOH-kwor"],["I like it","id mihi placet","id MI-hi PLAH-ket"],["I do not like it","id mihi non placet","id MI-hi nohn PLAH-ket"],["she is here","ea hic est","EH-ah heek est"],["she is not here","ea hic non est","EH-ah heek nohn est"],["I have a car","autocinetum habeo","ow-toh-KEE-neh-toom hah-BEH-oh"],["I do not have a car","autocinetum non habeo","ow-toh-KEE-neh-toom nohn hah-BEH-oh"],["I understand","intellego","in-TEL-leh-goh"],["I do not understand","non intellego","nohn in-TEL-leh-goh"],["we are tired","fessi sumus","FES-see SOO-moos"],["we are not tired","fessi non sumus","FES-see nohn SOO-moos"],["he works on Sundays","die Solis laborat","DEE-eh SOH-lis lah-BOH-raht"],["he does not work on Sundays","die Solis non laborat","DEE-eh SOH-lis nohn lah-BOH-raht"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Add -ne to the first word of the sentence for a yes-or-no question. Use \"nonne\" when you expect \"yes\" and \"num\" when you expect \"no\"."],"rows":[["statement","magister est","mah-GIS-ter est"],["question","estne magister?","EST-neh mah-GIS-ter"],["you expect yes","nonne magister est?","NOHN-neh mah-GIS-ter est"],["you expect no","num magister est?","noom mah-GIS-ter est"]],"ex":[["do you speak English?","loquerisne Anglice?","loh-KWEH-ris-neh AHN-gli-keh"],["is she a doctor?","estne ea medica?","EST-neh EH-ah MEH-di-kah"],["do you have a pen?","habesne stilum?","hah-BES-neh STEE-loom"],["are you tired?","esne fessus?","ES-neh FES-soos"],["is it far?","estne procul?","EST-neh PROH-kool"],["is the restaurant open?","estne caupona aperta?","EST-neh kow-POH-nah ah-PEHR-tah"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":[],"rows":[["what","quid","kwid"],["who","quis","kwis"],["where","ubi","OO-bi"],["when","quando","KWAHN-doh"],["why","cur","koor"],["how","quomodo","KWOH-moh-doh"],["which","qui / quae / quod","kwee / kwai / kwod"],["how much / how many","quantus / quot","KWAHN-toos / kwot"]],"ex":[["what is this?","quid est hoc?","kwid est hohk"],["who is she?","quae est ea?","kwai est EH-ah"],["where do you live?","ubi habitas?","OO-bi HAH-bi-tahs"],["when is the exam?","quando est examen?","KWAHN-doh est ek-SAH-men"],["why are you late?","cur serus es?","koor SEH-roos ehs"],["how much is it?","quanti constat?","KWAN-tee KON-stat"],["which book?","qui liber?","kwee LI-ber"]]},{"id":"possessives","title":"Possessives","text":["Meus (my), tuus (your), suus (his, her own), noster (our), vester (your, plural). They agree with the noun: liber meus, domus mea, nomen meum."],"rows":[["my","meus / mea / meum","MEH-oos / MEH-ah / MEH-oom"],["your (one person)","tuus / tua / tuum","TOO-oos"],["his / her","eius","EH-yoos"],["our","noster / nostra / nostrum","NOS-ter"],["their","eorum / earum","EH-oh-room"]],"ex":[["my house","domus mea","DOH-moos MEH-ah"],["your friends","amici tui","ah-MEE-kee TOO-ee"],["his sister","soror eius","SOH-ror EH-yoos"],["our teacher","magister noster","mah-GIS-ter NOS-ter"],["their car","autocinetum eorum","ow-toh-KEE-neh-toom EH-oh-room"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["Latin has no polite \"you\" for one person. Use \"domine\" (sir), \"domina\" (madam), \"quaeso\" (please) and the plural \"vos\" for respect to several people."],"rows":[["sir","domine","DOH-mi-neh"],["madam","domina","DOH-mi-nah"],["gentlemen","domini","DOH-mi-nee"],["good sir (very polite)","vir clarissime","wir klah-RIS-si-meh"]],"ex":[["you speak (to one person)","loqueris","loh-KWEH-ris"],["you speak (to several people)","loquimini","loh-KWI-mi-nee"],["you are tired (to one person)","fessus es","FES-soos ehs"],["you are tired (to several people)","fessi estis","FES-see ES-tis"],["thank you, sir","gratias, domine","GRAH-tee-ahs DOH-mi-neh"],["excuse me, madam","ignosce, domina","ig-NOS-keh DOH-mi-nah"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past (perfect): -avi, -avisti, -avit, -avimus, -avistis, -averunt for amare (amavi = I loved). Future: -bo, -bis, -bit, -bimus, -bitis, -bunt (amabo = I will love)."],"rows":[["I loved","amavi","ah-MAH-wee"],["you loved","amavisti","ah-mah-WIS-tee"],["he / she loved","amavit","ah-MAH-wit"],["I will love","amabo","ah-MAH-boh"],["we will love","amabimus","ah-MAH-bi-moos"]],"ex":[["yesterday I worked","heri laboravi","HEH-ri lah-boh-RAH-wee"],["she bought a book","librum emit","LEE-broom EH-mit"],["I will call you tomorrow","cras te vocabo","krahs teh woh-KAH-boh"],["we will eat at eight","hora octava cenabimus","HOH-rah ok-TAH-wah keh-NAH-bi-moos"],["they travelled to Spain","in Hispaniam iter fecerunt","in his-PAH-nee-ahm I-ter feh-KEH-roont"],["I went to the market","ad forum ivi","ad FOH-room EE-wee"],["he will come later","postea veniet","POS-teh-ah WEH-nee-et"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Command to one person: take off -re (ama!). To several: -te (amate!). Say \"do not\" with \"noli\" (one person) or \"nolite\" (several) plus the infinitive: noli venire!"],"rows":[["speak! (one person)","loquere!","LOH-kweh-reh"],["speak! (several)","loquimini!","loh-KWI-mi-nee"],["do not speak!","noli loqui!","NOH-lee LOH-kwee"]],"ex":[["come here","veni huc","WEH-nee hook"],["do not come here","noli huc venire","NOH-lee hook weh-NEE-reh"],["sit down","sede","SEH-deh"],["do not sit down","noli sedere","NOH-lee seh-DEH-reh"],["be quiet","tace","TAH-keh"],["do not be late","noli sero venire","NOH-lee SEH-roh weh-NEE-reh"],["open the door","aperi ianuam","AH-peh-ri YAH-noo-ahm"],["close the window","claude fenestram","KLOW-deh feh-NES-trahm"],["listen to me","audi me","OW-dee meh"],["do not worry","noli timere","NOH-lee ti-MEH-reh"],["speak slowly","loquere lente","LOH-kweh-reh LEN-teh"],["wait a moment","exspecta paulisper","eks-SPEK-tah pow-LIS-per"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["Possum (can), debeo (must), volo (want) are followed by an infinitive. Negative: add \"non\". Nolo = I do not want. Non licet = it is not allowed."],"rows":[["I can","possum","POS-soom"],["I must","debeo","deh-BEH-oh"],["I want","volo","WOH-loh"]],"ex":[["I can swim","natare possum","nah-TAH-reh POS-soom"],["I cannot swim","natare non possum","nah-TAH-reh nohn POS-soom"],["can you help me?","potesne me adiuvare?","poh-TES-neh meh ad-yoo-WAH-reh"],["we must go","ire debemus","EE-reh deh-BEH-moos"],["we must not go","non licet nobis ire","nohn LEE-ket NOH-bees EE-reh"],["I want to eat","edere volo","EH-deh-reh WOH-loh"],["I do not want to eat","edere nolo","EH-deh-reh NOH-loh"],["you can come","venire potes","weh-NEE-reh POH-tehs"],["you cannot come","venire non potes","weh-NEE-reh nohn POH-tehs"],["she wants to study","studere vult","STOO-deh-reh woolt"],["I must work today","hodie laborare debeo","HOH-dee-eh lah-boh-RAH-reh deh-BEH-oh"],["you must not run","non licet tibi currere","nohn LEE-ket TI-bi KOOR-reh-reh"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["Latin uses prepositions with cases. In + ablative = in / on (where): in mensa. In + accusative = into. Sub = under. Apud / prope = next to / near. Ad = to / at."],"rows":[["in / on (place)","in + ablative","in"],["under","sub","soob"],["next to","apud","AH-poohd"],["near","prope","PROH-peh"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","liber in mensa est","LI-ber in MEN-sah est"],["the cat is under the table","feles sub mensa est","FEH-lehs soob MEN-sah est"],["I am at school","in schola sum","in SKOH-lah soom"],["I am at home","domi sum","DOH-mee soom"],["the shop is next to the bank","taberna apud argentariam est","tah-BEHR-nah AH-poohd ahr-gen-TAH-ree-ahm est"],["the park is near the station","hortus publicus prope stationem est","HOR-toos POO-bli-koos PROH-peh stah-tee-OH-nem est"],["we meet in the morning","mane conveniemus","MAH-neh kon-weh-nee-EH-moos"],["the lesson is at nine","lectio hora nona est","LEK-tee-oh HOH-rah NOH-nah est"],["the key is in the bag","clavis in sacco est","KLAH-wis in SAHK-koh est"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["Add -ior to the adjective for \"more\" (maior = bigger). Add -issimus for \"most\" (maximus = the biggest). Than = \"quam\". Irregular: bonus, melior, optimus (good, better, best)."],"rows":[["bigger than","maior quam","MAH-yor kwahm"],["better","melior","MEH-lee-or"],["the biggest","maximus","MAHK-si-moos"],["worse","peior","PEH-yor"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","magnus, maior, maximus","MAHG-noos MAH-yor MAHK-si-moos"],["small, smaller, the smallest","parvus, minor, minimus","PAHR-woos MI-nor MI-ni-moos"],["this is better than that","hoc melius est quam illud","hohk MEH-lee-oos est kwahm IL-lood"],["this is worse than that","hoc peius est quam illud","hohk PEH-yoos est kwahm IL-lood"],["she is taller than me","altior est quam ego","AHL-tee-or est kwahm EH-goh"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Tashkentum maior est quam Samarcanda","tahsh-KEN-toom MAH-yor est kwahm sah-mahr-KAHN-dah"],["it is the cheapest","vilissimum est","wi-LIS-si-moom est"],["the same as","idem ac","EE-dem ahk"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Extra practice with the most useful patterns."],"rows":[],"ex":[["he is a teacher","magister est","mah-GIS-ter est"],["you (plural) are students","vos discipuli estis","wohs dis-KIP-oo-lee ES-tis"],["I am happy","laetus sum","LAI-toos soom"],["she is at school","in schola est","in SKOH-lah est"],["you are my friend","tu amicus meus es","too ah-MEE-koos MEH-oos ehs"],["it is cold","frigus est","FREE-goos est"],["I study English","linguam Anglicam disco","LIN-gwahm AHN-gli-kahm DIS-koh"],["he teaches maths","mathematicam docet","mah-theh-MAH-ti-kahm DOH-ket"],["they work every day","cotidie laborant","koh-TEE-dee-eh lah-BOH-rahnt"],["is this your book?","estne hic liber tuus?","EST-neh heek LI-ber TOO-oos"],["are they here?","suntne hic?","SOONT-neh heek"],["do you like tea?","placetne tibi thea?","plah-KET-neh TI-bi THEH-ah"],["what time is it?","quota hora est?","KWOH-tah HOH-rah est"],["whose book is this?","cuius liber est hic?","KOO-yoos LI-ber est heek"],["how old are you?","quot annos natus es?","kwot AHN-nohs NAH-toos ehs"],["how do you say it?","quomodo id dicis?","KWOH-moh-doh id DEE-kis"],["your book (formal)","liber tuus, domine","LI-ber TOO-oos DOH-mi-neh"],["their house","domus eorum","DOH-moos EH-oh-room"],["my phone","telephonum meum","teh-leh-PHOH-noom MEH-oom"],["excuse me, sir","ignosce, domine","ig-NOS-keh DOH-mi-neh"],["please sit down (formal)","sedete, quaeso","seh-DEH-teh KWAI-soh"],["come here (informal)","veni huc","WEH-nee hook"],["yesterday I was tired","heri fessus eram","HEH-ri FES-soos EH-rahm"],["I will study tomorrow","cras studebo","krahs stoo-DEH-boh"],["we went to the park","in hortum publicum ivimus","in HOR-toom POO-bli-koom ee-WEE-moos"]]}],"name":"Latin","id":"la","flag":"la","note":""}